# Case: Native second launch reopens the original window
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Isolate second-launch activation from the separately tested hidden-window capture requirement.
# Steps:
#   Close the focused task main window through physical Alt+F4; launch the same application identity; inspect the original window and service generation.
# Expected:
#   The second process exits successfully; the original service generation and window remain; fresh capture works after reopening; explicit Quit cleans both processes.
# Forbidden:
#   Claims that reopening proves capture while hidden, unrelated application activation or duplicate service owners.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D second launch baseline'
start
system-key Alt+F4
system-window unic hidden
system-second-launch
system-window unic visible
system-board-write 'UNIC-D second launch reopened 中文'
ui-wait listItem 'UNIC-D second launch reopened 中文'
history-count 1
screenshot original-window-reopened
